Day 2 of Python Full Stack

Today I learned about Python program execution, compilation, bytecode, Python Virtual Machine, interactive mode and script mode.

I practiced the following concepts with Python code:

print("Hello World")

a = 10
b = 20
print(a + b)

a, b, c = 10, 20, 30
print(a, b, c)

x = y = z = 100
print(x, y, z)

a = 10
print(a)
a = 100
print(a)

numbers = [10, 20]
numbers.append(30)
print(numbers)

name = "Python"
name = name + " Programming"
print(name)

I also learned about tokens and their five types: keywords, identifiers, literals, operators and delimiters.

I learned statements, variables, multiple assignment, reassignment, mutable and immutable objects, and rules for naming variables.

I also practiced interactive mode using the Python interpreter and script mode using .py files.

